# AI-native SDLC (project rule)

When doing non-trivial feature work, follow the tool-agnostic artifact loop:

1. Read [`docs/ai-sdlc/README.md`](docs/ai-sdlc/README.md).
2. Prefer templates under `docs/ai-sdlc/templates/` and live folders under `docs/ai-sdlc/features/<slug>/`.
3. Apply institutional skills in `docs/ai-sdlc/skills/` (offline-first, platform-channel-safety, cancellation-disposables, theme-tokens).
4. Prove with [`docs/ai-sdlc/gates.md`](docs/ai-sdlc/gates.md) — scripts + required CI — not vendor hook JSON.
5. Keep machine-checked AIDLC (`docs/ai/aidlc_workflow.md`) when T1/T2 lifecycle is active.

Do not create `CLAUDE.md` or `.claude/`. Entry map: `AGENTS.md`.
